00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,923
Diagnose behavior before attaching a label.

2
00:00:02,993 --> 00:00:08,795
The framework names eleven failures, including
parachuting, going native, silent assumptions,

3
00:00:08,865 --> 00:00:13,900
moving goalposts, fragile prototypes,
bespoke loops, and hero dependency.

4
00:00:13,970 --> 00:00:17,725
Use the symptom to select a
counter and an observable test.

5
00:00:17,795 --> 00:00:21,848
External review helps preserve
critical distance after immersion.

6
00:00:21,918 --> 00:00:27,443
Do not classify disagreement as going native
simply because a colleague challenges your

7
00:00:27,513 --> 00:00:28,857
proposed solution.

8
00:00:28,927 --> 00:00:32,511
The team removes the quality
threshold after errors appear.

9
00:00:32,581 --> 00:00:34,885
A prototype runs without an owner.

10
00:00:34,955 --> 00:00:38,347
Every rule change depends
on the original engineer.

11
00:00:38,417 --> 00:00:40,977
Each symptom maps to a different failure mode.

12
00:00:41,047 --> 00:00:45,826
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

13
00:00:45,896 --> 00:00:49,992
Name each failure, its counter, and
evidence that the counter worked.

14
00:00:50,062 --> 00:00:55,246
Moving goalposts: restore the timestamped
threshold and publish the complete result.

15
00:00:55,316 --> 00:01:00,521
Fragile prototype: hold landing until
an owner and support conditions exist.

16
00:01:00,591 --> 00:01:05,733
Hero dependency: teach the maintainer
and test an independent rule update.

17
00:01:05,803 --> 00:01:10,411
The correction needs behavior evidence,
not merely a newly written policy.

18
00:01:10,481 --> 00:01:12,870
Which symptom indicates moving goalposts?

19
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:15,628
A. Writing a prediction before acting B.

20
00:01:15,698 --> 00:01:17,746
Rejecting malformed input C.

21
00:01:17,816 --> 00:01:21,059
Changing success criteria after seeing results.

22
00:01:21,129 --> 00:01:22,537
The best answer is C.

23
00:01:22,607 --> 00:01:26,105
Post-result threshold changes
distort the experiment.
